            <ArticleTitle>Transient giant R waves--a manifestation of potentially reversible acute severe myocardial ischaemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>92-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with acute severe myocardial ischaemia manifested with transient giant R waves and ST segment elevation during chest pain. This probably represents transient complete occlusion of a major coronary artery, the left anterior descending in this case. Myocardial infarction was prevented by aggressive medical and surgical management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
